; SimConnect.cfg -- CLIENT-side config for PilotAI.Connector.exe
;
; This file belongs on the machine that RUNS PilotAI.Connector.exe -- NOT
; necessarily the same PC as Prepar3D. Copy it next to the built
; PilotAI.Connector.exe (same folder as the .exe) and rename it from
; "SimConnect.cfg.template" to "SimConnect.cfg".
;
; If the Connector runs directly on the same PC as Prepar3D, this file is
; not needed at all -- SimConnect defaults to a local connection with no
; config file present. Only add this file when the Connector runs on a
; DIFFERENT PC than Prepar3D, talking to it over the LAN.
;
; SimConnectReader.cs opens SimConnect with ConfigIndex 0
;   (new SimConnect(AppName, IntPtr.Zero, 0, _simConnectEvent, 0))
; which makes the SimConnect DLL itself read the [SimConnect] section below
; -- no PilotAI code change is needed to connect remotely.
;
; Replace UFLY_SIM_PC_LOCAL_IPV4 with the actual local IPv4 address of the
; Windows PC running Prepar3D at UFly (e.g. 192.168.1.42). Do not guess
; this value -- get it from the UFly sim PC itself (ipconfig) or from
; whoever manages that network.

[SimConnect]
Protocol=IPv4
Address=UFLY_SIM_PC_LOCAL_IPV4
Port=500
MaxReceiveSize=41088
DisableNagle=0
